{"results":[{"url":"https://www.forbes.com/real-time-billionaires/","final_url":"https://www.forbes.com/real-time-billionaires/","title":"Forbes Real Time Billionaires List - The World's Richest People","description":"Browse today’s rankings of the wealthiest people and families globally. Discover the net worth, age, and other information about the richest people in the world.","language":"en","text":"# The World’sReal-Time Billionaires\n\nThe definitive, minute-by-minute guide to every billionaire around the globe. See who's up, who's down and who's a new member of the three-comma club.\n\nLast UpdatedNov 03, 2026, 03:45am EST\n\n$2.534TTotal Wealth Of Women Billionaires\n\n$2.769TTotal Wealth Of Top 10\n\n$-12,985.7MWealth Gained By Top 10 In The Last 24 Hours\n\n1,461,748%Wealth Gap Between Average Billionaire And Average American\n\n1,609Billionaires Are Wealthier Today\n\n1,132Billionaires Are Less Wealthy Today\n\n$2.534TTotal Wealth Of Women Billionaires\n\n$2.769TTotal Wealth Of Top 10\n\n$-12,985.7MWealth Gained By Top 10 In The Last 24 Hours\n\n1,461,748%Wealth Gap Between Average Billionaire And Average American\n\n1,609Billionaires Are Wealthier Today\n\n1,132Billionaires Are Less Wealthy Today\n\n1.\n\n## Elon Musk\n\nCURRENT NET WORTH$878.5B\n\n-$62.1B (-6.61%)PAST WEEK\n\nWEALTH HISTORY\n\nData Shown in Eastern Time\n\nLATEST RELATED NEWS\n\n2.\n\n## Jeff Bezos\n\nCURRENT NET WORTH$366B\n\n-$4.6B (-1.24%)PAST WEEK\n\nWEALTH HISTORY\n\nData Shown in Eastern Time\n\nLATEST RELATED NEWS\n\n3.\n\n## Larry Page\n\nCURRENT NET WORTH$232.3B\n\n-$30.7B (-11.66%)PAST WEEK\n\nWEALTH HISTORY\n\nData Shown in Eastern Time\n\nLATEST RELATED NEWS\n\n4.\n\n## Michael Dell\n\nCURRENT NET WORTH$218.5B\n\n-$30.2B (-12.14%)PAST WEEK\n\nWEALTH HISTORY\n\nData Shown in Eastern Time\n\nLATEST RELATED NEWS\n\n5.\n\n## Sergey Brin\n\nCURRENT NET WORTH$213.9B\n\n-$28.2B (-11.64%)PAST WEEK\n\nWEALTH HISTORY\n\nData Shown in Eastern Time\n\nLATEST RELATED NEWS\n\n## Biggest Gainers\n\nGains reflect daily net worth changes\n\n1.\n\nElon Musk\n\n+$10B (+1.15%)\n\n2.\n\nMukesh Ambani\n\n+$8B (+10.00%)\n\n3.\n\nJeff Bezos\n\n+$4.7B (+1.29%)\n\n4.\n\nRob Walton & family\n\n+$3.8B (+2.58%)\n\n5.\n\nJim Walton & family\n\n+$3.8B (+2.63%)\n\n## Biggest Losers\n\nLosses reflect daily net worth changes\n\n1.\n\nLarry Ellison\n\n-$11.9B (-6.91%)\n\n2.\n\nMichael Dell\n\n-$9.9B (-4.34%)\n\n3.\n\nSteve Ballmer\n\n-$3.7B (-2.31%)\n\n4.\n\nChen Tianshi\n\n-$3B (-12.72%)\n\n5.\n\nMark Zuckerberg\n\n-$2.8B (-1.32%)\n\n## Methodology\n\nForbes’ Real-Time Billionaires ranking tracks the daily ups and downs of the world’s richest people. The wealth-tracking platform provides ongoing updates on the net worth and ranking of each individual confirmed by Forbes to be a billionaire. The value of individuals’ public holdings are updated every 5 minutes when respective stock markets are open (there will be a 15-minute delay for stock prices). Individuals whose fortunes are significantly tied to private companies will have their net worths updated once a day. Major private companies are adjusted according to an industry- or region-specific market index provided by our partners at FactSet Research Systems when available. Our biggest gainer and biggest loser data compares billionaires’ fortunes to the previous trading day’s market close. Our comparison of wealth to the typical American is based on a median U.S. household net worth of $211,000, based on a Federal Reserve survey, adjusted for inflation. The Forbes Philanthropy Score measures the lifetime, out-the-door charitable giving of billionaires who appear on The Forbes 400, ranked on a scale of 1 to 5 based on what percentage of their net worth they have donated to those in need. Our self-made score is scaled from 1 (heir who does not work to grow the fortune) to 10 (self-made who overcame substantial obstacles).","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":24107.527432001007,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}